From f6939175ae31d239d0f4e8c2dac596cd8651f331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:20:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(departments): stop activity article page hanging on
 missing slug
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The department-activity card list falls back to the document's raw
Sanity _id when its slug hasn't been generated, but the article-detail
page only ever queried by slug.current — so a broken/slug-less activity
would never resolve and the page hung on "Loading..." forever.

- Require the slug field in Studio so new activities can't be published
  without one.
- Make the detail query match by _id as a fallback, so already-published
  slug-less activities resolve immediately without needing a manual fix.
- Distinguish "still loading" from "fetched, found nothing" in
  useCmsDepartmentActivity/DepartmentActivityDetail, and show a proper
  not-found page (with a back link) instead of an indefinite spinner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012xNEugH42JGJDBqiHFtfyU
